# Key width decides how many facts live ([LFAC.1.7.2]), at key = one slot:
# one live fact per `a`. Asserting (1,"x"), (1,"x"), (1,"y") and (2,"x") leaves
# two facts: the second is a no-op reassert ([LFAC.2.5.1]) and the third a
# retract-and-replace ([LFAC.2.5.3]). `runtime/LFAC.1.7.2_key_all_relation` is
# the key = all case.
schema Pair scope logical:
    a: Int key
    b: String mutable
